# Canonical-form content digests — the digest of the bytes a registered
# WellBehavedLens emits after applying its source's canonical
# transformation (W3C XML Canonicalization 1.1 for USLM/XML sources,
# W3C RDF Dataset Canonicalization RDFC-1.0 N-Quads of the source
# graph for OWL/RDF sources, RFC 8785 JCS for JSON, Unicode NFKC for
# plain text, etc.). Drift in the lens implementation or in the
# canonical form surfaces here while the raw-bytes hash above remains
# stable. The
# `formal::meta::well_behaved_lens::harness::RoundTripHarnessAllVerified`
# axiom verifies these match on every test run.
[canonical_signatures]
# No USC title carries a canonical signature anymore: ALL nine are byte-exact
# graph-faithful (SLICE U8 flipped the last floor title, usc_title_49, to the
# `UslmGraphFaithfulLens`), so each now pins a `[byte_exact_signatures]` entry
# instead. The floor `UslmXmlLens` canonical form (xml-c14n-1.1, Boyer & Marcy
# 2008) is no longer the registered tier for any title.
# OWL vocabularies — OwlLens canonical form is the W3C RDF Dataset
# Canonicalization (RDFC-1.0, REC-rdf-canon-20240521 §1.1/§4.4.3)
# serialized canonical N-Quads of the *source RDF graph*
# (`read_owl_to_quads(bytes)`, the raw triple stream below the
# OwlOntology projection). This pins RDF GRAPH identity (RDF 1.1
# Concepts §3.6 graph isomorphism; Hogan 2017): isomorphic graphs
# canonicalize byte-identically. It is NOT OWL-structural identity
# (OWL 2 Structural Spec §3 — deferred) nor logical/entailment
# identity (never pinned). Term-level caveat: RDFC fixes blank-node
# *arrangement*, not literal lexical forms ("1"^^xsd:int ≠
# "01"^^xsd:int). The six vocabs DO carry blank nodes (cito 9, doco
# 287, c4o 21, biro 16, prov_o 68, olia 317 — from rdf:nodeID,
# parseType="Collection", owl:unionOf/intersectionOf/Restriction), so
# RDFC's blank-node labelling is load-bearing here. It also fixes the
# old lossy `write_owl(read_owl(bytes))` typed-view re-emission (which
# dropped 24–1187 triples/vocab) and is the W3C-standard graph-identity
# grounding, now checked by the live `.prx` load-gate canonical leg:
# drift in ANY source triple (not just the typed-view subset) surfaces.
"cito@2.8.1"             = "blake3:1dd88227c285e03ee857833dc83cee4722f2acfc87563a685bd9f5a6ed40ef89"
"doco@1.3"               = "blake3:6a74ae4591f2a55b915cc130da9f3e6050a2c5cd3752d022d87a675a2f114494"
"c4o@1.2"                = "blake3:6316fc9ed707ae37b6697b6836d63204f646b40b1f543dfadafa7b3b1d2157f5"
"biro@1.1.1"             = "blake3:2a3a661e9bb893268e035c96d700e27c0f2dc16f1ac49488ed3bfd16306497ee"
"prov_o@2013-04-30"      = "blake3:5bc8fc7f7a43d6d6e08a621b52210440eab5b9da01a75764e61961cdb5ce2488"
"olia@2026-04-09"        = "blake3:4b33405f21491496496e3f79bd9bad1d444a3d6b7627290155fa49b0fa8dcdcc"

# Archive content addresses — the content digest of the rkyv `.prx` envelope bytes
# (the `BinaryEnvelope` MerkleRoot) for each source's compiled archive.
# Distinct from `[hashes]` (the raw source) and `[canonical_signatures]`
# (the lens output): this pins the *compiled archive itself*, and is the
# integrity claim the `.prx` load gate re-derives from the envelope bytes
# and verifies before installing anything (W3C Subresource Integrity 2016;
# Dolstra 2006 content-addressing; Merkle 1987).
#
# STEP-0 DOCTRINE — this is a per-toolchain BUILD-OUTPUT / CACHE pin, NOT the
# source's durable identity. It changes whenever the rkyv crate version /
# features, the rkyv on-disk layout, or the projected data changes — so it is
# re-pinned mechanically from the value `dump_archive_addresses` (OWL/USC) /
# `dump_wordnet_archive_addresses` (WordNet) reports, and the
# `archive_anchors_match_lock` / `wordnet_archive_anchors_match_lock` /
# `usc_archive_anchors_match_lock` tests guard every pinned source. The DURABLE
# identity of a source is `[hashes]` (the raw source content) and, for a
# round-trip-pinned source, `[canonical_signatures]` (the lens canonical form)
# or `[byte_exact_signatures]` (the strict byte-exact round-trip = the raw
# hash). A CI guard asserts the rkyv crate version + features so a silent
# dependency bump that would invalidate every archive pin is caught (see
# `rkyv_archive_format_version_guard` in owl/prx.rs). Written by
# `pr4xis compile --lock` after every emitted archive round-trip-loads
# through the fail-closed gate.
[archive_signatures]
"biro@1.1.1"             = "blake3:0dcb74b14435134365fd1aadb6895332a9923b64c9608c6cbe79308ee6af398e"
"c4o@1.2"                = "blake3:cad877820b5b767f738f7faf94fa816ab60b5cb84898467b9d32ebe46e19d180"
"cito@2.8.1"             = "blake3:5034ec4b534cbbf093a31f9b52560cd2a4858f75fdebad6098009182cec2dee7"
"doco@1.3"               = "blake3:aea6fa2dbb0c294b1589231b59d5bd7185526bb32eee7d111b7b1a4900fe865c"
"olia@2026-04-09"        = "blake3:c977889ccece56015e78039c78c3a0eccbe54a93248f029bdb2a3b4ca370f93b"
"prov_o@2013-04-30"      = "blake3:280de220aa9e3f77518877b8f1dcaf1fa519ffc2f19a1f5b79173a0378004a78"
